{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Deliver me, I pray, from the hand of</b> — ר\"ת המן. An allusion to Haman, who set out to strike אם על בנים, as written: טף ונשים (children and women)." "<b>And prepare me</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other: אם יוכל להלחם אתי והכני, regarding Goliath — to teach: just as Jacob feared, so David feared; just as Jacob was pursued, so David was pursued; and just as Jacob was saved from Esau, so David was saved from Goliath; and the merit of Jacob stood for David. And just as with David there was battle, so Jacob prepared himself for battle — for he prepared himself for three things." "<b>אם על בנים</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other: אם על בנים רוטשה, in Sennacherib king of Assyria, who said to destroy Israel like Esau who came to fight with Jacob. And likewise: לא תקח האם על הבנים — an allusion to the exiles."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "ר\"ת = rashei tevot (initial letters). The three initial letters of הצילני נא מיד spell המן."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:35.668533608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}